    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, and every value derived from it moves to that new identity.\n\n**`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** (`rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`) \u2014 rewrote the code generation:\n- **REGION** = region code derived from the owner's postcode via `PostcodeRegions.regionForPostcode(...)` (NSW/VIC/QLD ranges), falling back to `UNKNOWN`.\n- **HASH8** = the first 8 upper-case hex characters (first 4 bytes) of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)` over UTF-8 bytes. By this pipeline step the telephone is already E.164-normalized by `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`.\n- Dropped the per-city sequence entirely, so it no longer needs `OwnerRepository` or any owner count.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.locality`** (`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`) \u2014 now derives locality as the REGION prefix of the `customerCode` (the part before the first `-`), instead of independently re-deriving from postcode/city. This keeps locality consistent with the new identity, returning `UNKNOWN` when the code is absent or has no region prefix.\n\n**Membership number, check digit, and the create audit record** already read `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so they automatically reflect the new region-and-hash identity \u2014 no logic change needed. The audit output confirms it: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` passes (code matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`), and the full suite is green (255 tests, 0 failures).",
